# Required for production — the CRM endpoint leads POST to.
# Until set, /api/lead logs non-PII lead context and returns ok so the form works in dev.
CURBIO_CRM_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Optional — sent as `Authorization: Bearer <key>` if present.
CURBIO_CRM_API_KEY=

# Optional — CookieYes site ID (CookieYes dashboard → the sell.curbio.com
# site entry → "Custom-coded site" install snippet — the ID is the path
# segment in that snippet's script src, e.g. .../client_data/<ID>/script.js).
# Renders the consent banner and enables CookieYes's own GPC handling. Absent
# in any environment (dev or prod) = no banner; see lib/consent.ts for how
# the rest of the app behaves with no banner ever having run (CONSENT_DEFAULT).
NEXT_PUBLIC_COOKIEYES_ID=

# Optional — Upstash Redis (Vercel Marketplace integration, installed with
# custom prefix "UPSTASH_REDIS_REST" — hence the doubled "REST" below; these
# are the two auto-provisioned vars for the read-write REST API, not the
# sibling _KV_URL/_REDIS_URL (different protocols) or _READ_ONLY_TOKEN).
# When set, every valid lead is durably persisted (LPUSH leads:v1, capped at
# 5000) BEFORE the visitor gets ok:true, and its delivery outcome is recorded
# afterwards in the leads:delivery:v1 hash, keyed by the lead's leadId.
# Absent = dev mode: log-and-continue, no persistence. There is deliberately NO rate limit on /api/lead — see the
# header comment in app/api/lead/route.ts before adding any submission guard.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_KV_REST_API_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_KV_REST_API_TOKEN=

# Optional — PostHog project API key (PostHog → Project Settings → Project API
# key). Absent = PostHog no-ops entirely, in every environment, with no crash.
# PostHog is consent-gated like Clarity, NOT like GA4: it has no cookieless
# mode, so it is never initialised until analytics consent is true and opts out
# if consent is withdrawn. See lib/posthog.ts and lib/consent.ts.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=
# Optional — defaults to https://us.i.posthog.com. Set for EU or self-hosted.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=

# ── /admin authentication ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Accounts live in Redis (lib/adminAuth.ts) — people sign up at /admin/signup
# and choose their own password. There is no per-person env var. The owner
# allowlist (who auto-approves on first signup) is in config/adminAccess.ts,
# in version control, since an email address isn't a secret.
#
# The one secret still needed: signs the session cookie. Not tied to any
# individual's credentials — rotating it just signs everyone out.
# Generate: python3 -c "import secrets;print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET=

# ── /admin page stats — Vercel Web Analytics ─────────────────────────────────
# Read-only traffic for the Pages screen. Absent = every view figure renders an
# em-dash, honestly, rather than a zero. The screen still works.
#
# GET ONE:  vercel.com → avatar (top right) → Account Settings → Tokens →
#           "Create Token". Name it `curbio-web page-stats`. SCOPE: pick the
#           `curbio` TEAM, not your personal account — the project lives under
#           the team (see DECISIONS.md). Expiration: your call; a rotated token
#           just makes views em-dash until it is replaced.
#
# NOTE: the Vercel CLI's own session token (~/Library/Application Support/
# com.vercel.cli/auth.json) is NOT this. It is short-lived and will start
# returning 403 invalidToken within hours. Create a real account token.
#
# TEAM_ID and PROJECT_ID are NOT secrets — they are the two values already in
# .vercel/project.json (gitignored, so DECISIONS.md carries them too).
#
# API traps, both of which return 200 with a WRONG answer — see
# lib/vercelAnalytics.ts:
#   • date params are `since`/`until`; `from`/`to` are silently ignored
#   • the grouping param is `by`; `groupBy` is silently ignored
#   • visits/aggregate caps BUCKETS, not date range: 62 at day granularity, so
#     90d must use week buckets and say so
VERCEL_API_TOKEN=
VERCEL_TEAM_ID=
VERCEL_PROJECT_ID=

# ── /admin page stats — GA4 (the second view source) ─────────────────────────
# Vercel counts raw pageviews server-side; GA4 models consent-denied visitors
# under Consent Mode v2. They disagree, and the dashboard shows both, labelled,
# and never averages them. Absent = the GA4 column stays an em-dash.
#
# GET ONE — four steps, and step 3 is the one people miss:
#   1. console.cloud.google.com → create or pick a project → APIs & Services →
#      Library → search "Google Analytics Data API" → Enable.
#   2. Same project → IAM & Admin → Service Accounts → Create Service Account.
#      Name it `curbio-ga4-reader`. No project roles are needed — the grant
#      that matters is step 3, on the GA4 property, not on the GCP project.
#   3. Copy the service account's email (…iam.gserviceaccount.com), then go to
#      analytics.google.com → Admin → Property access management → "+" → add
#      that email with the **Viewer** role. Without this every call 403s.
#   4. Back in the service account → Keys → Add Key → Create new → JSON.
#
# Paste the JSON key as a SINGLE LINE below. Vercel env vars cannot hold real
# newlines, so keep the \n escapes inside private_key exactly as the file has
# them — do not expand them.
#
# GA4_PROPERTY_ID is the numeric property id (Admin → Property details), NOT
# the G-XXXXXXX measurement id that NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID uses.
GA4_PROPERTY_ID=
GA4_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=

# ── /admin Ask panel — Anthropic ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Powers the Ask box on Today and the CMO Outlook. Absent = the panel renders
# a disabled state saying so, rather than failing at submit.
#
# GET ONE:  console.anthropic.com → Settings → API Keys → Create Key.
# The key is server-side only and must never carry a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix — the
# route at app/api/admin/ask/route.ts is the only thing that reads it.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
